  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OffsetPerRowOrCol::apply",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/common/DngOpcodes.cpp",
    "description": "Heap-buffer-overflow is caused by out-of-bounds indexing into delta arrays in DNG DeltaPerColumn/DeltaPerRow opcode application. In OffsetPerRowOrCol<S>::apply, the code uses this->deltaI[S::select(x,y)] (or deltaF) for every pixel coordinate in ROI, but never validates that the opcode-provided deltaF_count matches the accessed coordinate range (width for SelectX / height for SelectY). As a result, crafted opcode data with too-short delta array leads to OOB read during applyOpCodes().",
    "conditions": "From the TIFF/DNG input, the harness reaches DngDecoder::handleMetadata(), which constructs DngOpcodes from OPCODELIST1 and calls applyOpCodes() after decodeData. A PoV must include a DeltaPerColumn opcode (code 11; crash shows SelectX) with deltaF_count smaller than the ROI/image width (or similarly DeltaPerRow smaller than height). During OffsetPerRowOrCol::apply -> PixelOpcode::applyOP loop over ROI pixels, S::select(x,y) exceeds deltaI/deltaF size, triggering heap OOB read."
  },
